From the lib/ review after k5 (repro scripts in the session scratchpad: stop.pl, scaled.pl, borrowed.pl, restart.pl). (1) After stop or a manual kubectl scale to 0, reconcile reports Running and never scales back: _workload_problem compares ready replicas with the live spec.replicas (0 counts as healthy), and _stopped gives up once it sees a DaemonSet/ReplicaSet/bare Pod. The POD promises "a reconcile after stop deploys again". Fix: judge replicas against the rendered (desired) manifests where known, so a workload below its desired replicas is not healthy (phase Stopped when scaled to 0); a manifest that itself says replicas 0 must not loop. (2) Borrow -> local switch can leave the bridge in place while reporting Running: the guard looks at the previous status.upstream, which early-stopping steps (Disabled, Blocked, NeedsConfig) erase. SPEC §6 also wants status.upstream/status.endpoints kept while an upstream is active. Fix: carry status.upstream and status.endpoints forward in early-stop phases like managedResources. (3) Pruning debt is never paid: a healthy local Comb goes straight to Running, so a failed prune (kept in managedResources) or a resource dropped from manifests is never pruned while healthy (k4 open point 1). Fix: when healthy but the rendered set differs from managedResources (group/kind/namespace/name), deploy + prune (phase per your judgement, report it). Content-only changes (e.g. new image tag) stay out of scope - flag for the maintainer. (4) A reconcile during a rolling restart undoes it: ensure replaces the object with the rendered manifest and drops the <prefix>restartedAt pod-template annotation, so every restart causes a second rollout. Fix: deploy carries a live restartedAt annotation over into the rendered pod template of Deployment/StatefulSet/DaemonSet. Regression test for each (they must fail before the fix).

